  "answer": "Blore, employed at the Deanery, discovers The Dean's secret betting on the horse Dandy Dick and his own poisoning of Dandy Dick to ensure his own horse Bonny-Betsy wins. The Dean, burdened by bills, refuses Sheba and Salome's request for money, which leads to their actions. The sequence is: The Dean's financial distress from bills causes him to refuse Sheba's request for money; Blore, aware of The Dean's betting, poisons Dandy Dick to secure his own bet on Bonny-Betsy.",
